{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793962022,"nonce":"0nBeOEuKtBBvceDdwWqUQiHD0zo=","title":"CI regressions in component tests and versioned book assembly","message":"Reproduced the latest main-branch failures on 13755915ac3be127d66523bb518f9f72529302bb (2026-11-06). CI https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/actions/runs/42192713856 failed across Linux/macOS/Windows tests; coverage https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/actions/runs/42192713817 and Android host tests https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/actions/runs/42192713811 shared failures. Documentation https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/actions/runs/42192713793 stopped during released-book restoration. iOS compile, Android target builds, WASM and the existing hosted Clippy job passed.\n\nGrouped fixes implemented locally, uncommitted:\n- The checked-checkbox, active-navigation and selected-tree tests used normal application rules to mark states now protected by important component rules. Their marker rules now explicitly use the same component layer/importance and sufficient specificity, preserving their original state/binding assertions. The separate selected-style tests still verify protection from ordinary app colour rules.\n- All selected-style headless scenarios now check adapter availability instead of panicking on coverage hosts; the static guard test passes unchanged.\n- The virtual-list integration test initializes its own theme, so it runs independently in nextest rather than relying on an earlier case.\n- Catalog CSS extraction normalizes checkout CRLF before locating Rust raw-string literals. A regression converts both real UA and CN source files to CRLF and verifies identical extraction. This addresses the six extra Windows failures.\n- mdBook leaves chapter-relative iframe URLs in the combined print page. The edition builder now rebases only print-page local example iframe sources to the snapshot root before freezing/checksumming. Missing assets still fail validation; external frames, escaped code, query strings, fragments and individual chapter pages stay intact. Regression freezes/verifies the corrected print page and rejects a missing demo.\n\nScoped verification: 11 CN cases including a new checkbox activation and two slider semantic regressions; 37 recorder/keyboard cases using the same isolated-process nextest model as CI; 9 catalog style/page checks including CRLF; the virtual-list endpoint test; 8 shared semantic tests; 15 book/release Python checks and 2 Simulator-runner checks pass. Actual current and v0.6.0-tag mdBook builds pass; all47 print iframe paths in each resolve within that edition (129 current pages,122 released pages), without rebuilding the48 WASM demos or uploading any archives.\n\nRelated accessibility validation uncovered and fixed a local checkbox regression: forwarding the row handler allowed a box click to toggle twice through bubbling. A shared per-click guard now consumes that bubbled copy while preserving box, label, keyboard and assistive actions and callback-once behavior. Core/CN regression and final iOS4/4 cover this; detailed accessibility work stays on26f0d537b927ce245f696edd00b54ddddf5aac6c24a8cd591eef3787b755ff2e. Selected-style contract stays on08f9941e60f97b301cb164e5ddf703520c67fddce84eb062fecabd404454c839; versioned book work on22802da4e63b5705b860f9162972406d5909ac29c9402a116cc4fd28bf483e46.\n\nEvidence: /private/tmp/blinc-ci-a11y-{cn-accessibility,controls}.log; /private/tmp/blinc-ci-fix-{catalog,virtual-list,semantics-final,book-tests,runner-tests}.log; /private/tmp/blinc-ci-book-{rebased,v060}/. Final iOS result target/ios-accessibility/results-1793961808062820000.xcresult has4 passes and no failures/skips/expected failures; Simulator shutdown_returncode0.\n\nRelease parent76a15bcfbb889c0af7e9ee97bf54cc40488a573eeaa0f92d136b0a6b3c1a32b6. All Cargo builds use jobs2 and gates stay scoped. No workflow exclusions, expected-failure